WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.950
Treasure Island

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:08.460
Fifteen men...

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:12.150
...on a dead man's chest!

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.780
Yo-ho-ho!
...And a bottle of rum!

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:19.890
<i>Everything is going well for now!</i>

00:00:20.790 --> 00:00:24.830
<i>During a huge storm,
we came across a ghost ship.</i>

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:28.920
<i>Then pirates attacked us.</i>

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:35.180
<i>This voyage is not without risks.</i>

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:41.600
<i>But...</i>

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:43.270
<i>Despite all that...</i>

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.590
<i>I think that it's going well at the moment.</i>

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:01.350
Here, Silver.
This'll be dessert.

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:02.910
Thanks.

00:01:03.670 --> 00:01:07.470
Say, Silver. There's a question I've been asking myself for a while.

00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:10.960
Why is this barrel of apples on deck?

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.210
There's a good reason. It's sort of a custom during long voyages.

00:01:15.210 --> 00:01:19.550
On the sea, if you don't eat fruits or vegetables, you become sick.

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:23.390
Even for the smallest injury,
the blood never stops flowing.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:28.510
So by placing a barrel on deck,
everyone can eat an apple...

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.510
...whenever they want.

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.570
Ah, I see.
So that's the reason.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.980
Treasure
Island

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.780
Takarajima

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.590
saa ikou

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:57.590
Come, let's go

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.680
yume ni mita shima heto

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:00.680
To the island that I've dreamed of

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.520
nami wo koete kaze ni notte

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:04.520
Across the waves, on the wind

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.400
umi hedeyou

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.400
We'll travel the oceans

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.320
ikute ni wa

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.320
Many of us

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:13.320
minna mada shiranai

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:13.320
Still don't know of

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.070
fushigi na hiru to yoru toga

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.070
The days and nights full of mystery

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.570
matte iru darou

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:19.570
That await us there

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.080
itsumo shinji you

00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:23.080
We must always have trust

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.330
magokoro wo

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.330
And be sincere

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:32.590
yuuki wo mune ni susumou yo

00:02:26.830 --> 00:02:32.590
And have courage in our hearts to move forward

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.720
tade hitotsu no

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:35.720
I only...

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.140
akogare dake wa

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.140
...have one desire

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.430
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:39.390 --> 00:02:41.430
And no one...

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.140
kese wa shinai sa

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:48.140
...will ever take it away

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.690
tade hitotsu no

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:54.690
I only...

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.990
akogare dake wa

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:57.990
...have one desire

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.320
doko no dare ni mo

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.320
And no one...

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:07.250
kese wa shinai sa

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:07.250
...will ever take it away

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:18.390
episode

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:18.390
Heard from the Inside
\h    of an Apple Barrel !

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.680
Here's the current position of the Hispaniola.

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.760
From now on, we'll be moving away from the equator...

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:34.610
...and take the trade winds towards the South.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:37.730
That way, if everything goes as planned,

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.450
we'll reach the island in three days.

00:03:41.800 --> 00:03:43.190
What, three days?

00:03:43.190 --> 00:03:45.440
You hear that, Livesey?

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:48.370
Incredible.
It's going faster than I thought.

00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:54.590
Silver! Silver!

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:58.590
Silver!

00:03:58.590 --> 00:03:59.640
Where is he?

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:03.240
Silver!

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.860
Silver!

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.350
You haven't seen Silver, have you?

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:11.690
Jim!

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.580
Silver was going towards the bow earlier.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:16.940
Thanks, Puppy!

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:22.500
There he is!

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.880
Silver!
Hey, listen to this!

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.000
Don't get too excited, Jim.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:36.380
The island will soon be in sight, right?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:39.300
Wow!
How did you know, Silver?

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:44.960
They were the ones who told me.

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:52.930
The seagulls?

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:57.280
There have been more and more seagulls starting two or three days ago.

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.900
When there are a lot of them,
it's a sign that land is near.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:16.400
So, Jim. How many days does the Captain think it'll be?

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.920
If all goes well, three days.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.130
Three days...

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.850
What is it Hands?
What are you doing here?

00:05:31.240 --> 00:05:33.940
Nothing. I, too, was coming to see the seagulls.

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.840
<i>It's been exactly 45 days since we left Bristol.</i>

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:42.370
<i>Our dear Hispaniola...</i>

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:45.440
<i>...is now very close to Treasure Island.</i>

00:05:45.440 --> 00:05:47.840
<i>My blood boiled, my heart pounded,</i>

00:05:47.840 --> 00:05:50.530
<i>I'm so excited that I can hardly sleep anymore.</i>

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:15.100
<i>Mother, if I were to become rich,
what would we do with the gold?</i>

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.840
Mother, I'm going to reconstruct the Admiral Benbow Inn!

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.530
Reconstruct it, Jim?
And what will it look like?

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:29.450
That's obvious. A luxury hotel, visible from miles around!

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:38.200
Whad'ya say, mother?
Impressed?

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:40.580
Jim, where do I find my room?

00:06:40.580 --> 00:06:41.670
That's obvious.

00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:44.550
In the tallest tower, where you will have the most beautiful view.

00:06:45.840 --> 00:06:48.000
Come on, mother.
This way.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:50.880
There are a lot of steps.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:54.100
There's no other path.
Come on, just a little more.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.320
What'd I tell you, mom?
Pretty view, right?

00:06:57.320 --> 00:07:01.000
It's magnificent, Jim.
Thank you so much.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:03.720
Nah, it was nothing.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:07.070
Wait, what's that noise?

00:07:10.920 --> 00:07:11.990
Jim!

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:14.120
Mother!

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.300
"Seagull" Puppy?

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.640
You have a minute?
I have to talk to you.

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:36.560
Talk to me, in the middle of the night?

00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:41.360
He's planning something terrible.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.440
Something terrible?

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.480
Listen up. Hands, the helmsman,
you know who he is?

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:48.530
Well, yeah.

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:52.200
At night, he rounds up everyone.

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:54.040
He's planning something secret.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.910
Something secret?

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:59.500
Surely, they're planning a mutiny.

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:00.970
What, a mutiny?!

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:05.130
Jim, this way.

00:08:06.080 --> 00:08:07.020
Over here, this way!

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:10.160
Hey...
Wh-Where are we going?

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:12.050
Don't worry.
Come on, follow me!

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:22.780
Wh-Where are we?

00:08:22.780 --> 00:08:26.560
We are in the hold. You've never been here before, right?

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:27.390
Nope.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:36.410
It's here. In this storeroom is where it happens.

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.480
Here, take a peek.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:42.600
Now, do you see anything strange among all those crates?

00:08:42.600 --> 00:08:44.320
Yeah, there's a light.

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:47.460
No, look harder.
Don't you see anyone?

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.360
I see, b-but that's...!

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:52.420
Yeah, it's him.
Hands, the helmsman.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:56.340
There's also Anderson, the bosun.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:59.310
And then, there's...

00:08:59.310 --> 00:09:00.620
Damn!

00:09:01.220 --> 00:09:03.240
The crates are blocking my view.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:06.230
Anyway, I'm not sure about the others.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:11.190
There were at least a dozen among those crates.

00:09:11.190 --> 00:09:14.400
But how can you be sure that they're planning a mutiny?

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.240
Listen, my experience as a sailor has taught me this:

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:20.490
A secret meeting of more
than five men is suspicious.

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:25.960
What'll we do?

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.420
What <i>can </i> we do, Jim?

00:09:28.310 --> 00:09:29.380
What should we do?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.710
Which side will you choose?

00:09:33.020 --> 00:09:34.220
What do you mean?

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:35.920
Don't play dumb, Jim.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.840
Will you join Hands or the Captain?

00:09:38.840 --> 00:09:41.200
You have to choose a side.

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:43.280
After all, there is a treasure to find.

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:46.840
So, you must really think about the situation.

00:09:46.840 --> 00:09:49.520
Unbelievable!
That's what you think?

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:52.170
Naturally! A man must think of himself first!

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.550
Because he's the most important.

00:09:57.820 --> 00:09:58.910
What?

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.660
Hands, the helmsman, planning a mutiny?

00:10:02.630 --> 00:10:03.000
Yeah.

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:05.450
Who told you such nonsense?

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:10.000
"Seagull" Puppy did.
He and I saw them last night.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.920
They're meeting in the storeroom of the hold.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:26.850
So Jim, have you talked to Dr. Livesey or the Captain?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:30.010
No, I wanted to talk to you first, Silver.

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:31.650
I see, good.

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:43.240
Well, alright.
I'll take a look tonight.

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:44.890
Yeah, really?

00:10:44.890 --> 00:10:46.690
Leave it to me.
Wanna tag along, Jim?

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:48.490
Yes, of course!

00:10:49.090 --> 00:10:51.050
Okay, Silver, see you tonight.

00:11:00.770 --> 00:11:02.220
Pardon me!

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:07.210
I-I'm sorry, Mr. Hands.

00:11:07.810 --> 00:11:12.970
Hey, Jim.
You were with Barbecue, right?

00:11:15.690 --> 00:11:19.210
By the way, you wouldn't happen to know what's on the menu tonight?

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.490
I-I think it's salted boiled potatoes.

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:25.080
What, again?
What rotten luck.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.290
Let's go, Benbow.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:55.770
Where are you going?

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:57.590
I'm going to the bathroom.

00:11:57.590 --> 00:11:59.280
You too, Benbow?

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:01.290
Alright, good night.

00:12:01.910 --> 00:12:03.240
Good night.

00:12:12.030 --> 00:12:12.710
Silver!

00:12:12.710 --> 00:12:13.290
Silver!

00:12:13.290 --> 00:12:13.620
Silver!

00:12:14.470 --> 00:12:17.050
That you, Jim?
Come in.

00:12:17.550 --> 00:12:20.510
But don't we have to go take a look in the storeroom?

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:22.470
We'll be going.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:24.930
However, we have to avoid the hallways.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:28.600
We're going to take a shortcut.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:29.890
A shortcut?

00:12:31.850 --> 00:12:36.750
By passing under the kitchen floor,
we'll be right on top of the storeroom.

00:12:36.750 --> 00:12:38.820
I see, you know your stuff.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:48.870
Rats.

00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:52.310
As long as the rats don't leave the ship,

00:12:52.310 --> 00:12:54.670
we don't have to worry.

00:12:54.670 --> 00:12:56.040
Really, is that so?

00:12:59.390 --> 00:13:01.910
Alright, it's over there.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:10.870
Let's see how they'll start the mutiny.

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:12.600
I'll go first.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:19.510
And, Silver?
What are they planning?

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:24.030
Hey, Jim.
This is one strange mutiny.

00:13:24.990 --> 00:13:26.320
Go on, have a look.

00:13:32.200 --> 00:13:35.390
Come on, two more laps!
Faster! Faster!

00:13:35.390 --> 00:13:38.750
Hey, hang in there, Number 3.
I bet 6 cents on you!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:39.720
Go! Move!

00:13:40.140 --> 00:13:42.590
Go, last lap!
Go, my pretty!

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:50.030
Dear Mother, this isn't right!

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:51.260
I won!

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:55.630
How clever of Number 3! She took advantage!

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.730
Strange mutiny, indeed.

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:04.690
What?
A turtle race?

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:07.990
Yeah, it was funny.
Silver and I had a good laugh.

00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:11.350
But if that's the case,
why do it in the storeroom?

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:14.610
After all, if the captain
caught them betting,

00:14:14.610 --> 00:14:16.210
they'd be in big trouble.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:17.390
Yeah, you're right.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:36.520
Silver, what are you looking at?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:38.370
The sunset.

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:39.880
The sunset?

00:14:40.840 --> 00:14:42.310
It's beautiful.

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:44.730
The sky is all red!
It looks like it's burning.

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.490
It's magnificent.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:49.700
I thought like you, when I was your age.

00:14:50.390 --> 00:14:52.660
But today, I don't like it as much.

00:14:53.430 --> 00:14:57.630
It can touch the heart
of a man in an instant,

00:14:58.150 --> 00:15:01.580
before it hides immediately
to make room for the night.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:04.550
Beware of such beauty.

00:15:06.190 --> 00:15:08.030
The sunset is a traitor.

00:15:08.030 --> 00:15:11.870
It can tip our hearts into darkness in an instant.

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:15.870
Becoming an adult, I finally understood...

00:15:15.870 --> 00:15:17.930
As a result, I hated sunsets.

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:21.900
If that's so, then why do you keep looking at them?

00:15:22.270 --> 00:15:26.150
Because even though I'm aware of it,
they're still beautiful.

00:15:26.150 --> 00:15:28.110
And so, I won't give in.

00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:30.280
I test my resistance.

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:55.300
My, my, if it itsn't helmsman Hands.
Good evening...

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:00.480
Come with me, please.
We have to talk.

00:16:00.480 --> 00:16:01.670
Talk?

00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:02.980
You mean...

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:04.550
Not here, come.

00:16:04.550 --> 00:16:05.800
Okay, sure.

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:19.610
<i>Mom, I'm currently having trouble getting to sleep.</i>

00:16:19.610 --> 00:16:21.250
<i>I guess it's not surprising.</i>

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:25.250
<i>Because Treasure Island is only one or two days away.</i>

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:29.230
Mother, look over there!
That's it! It's Treasure Island!

00:16:29.830 --> 00:16:31.670
It's fantastic, Jim!

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:35.510
So there really is an island full of treasure?

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:39.070
I told you there was!
So mother, what would you like?

00:16:39.070 --> 00:16:40.910
A pearl necklace?

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:44.390
Or crystal boots.
They're neat, eh?

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:46.030
Or maybe this gold lamp?

00:16:46.030 --> 00:16:49.130
If you put this on the inn,
it'll impress everyone in Black Hill!

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.910
Dear mother, can you give this to Lily for me?

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.060
Sure, you can count on me, Jim.

00:17:04.430 --> 00:17:05.630
Hey, Jim!

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:07.920
The golden soup is ready!
Come eat!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.690
Okay, Silver!

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:12.510
Oh right, Mother, I'll introduce you.

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.340
This man is named Silver.

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:18.830
He's the most courageous man on the Hispaniola and the nicest, too.

00:17:18.830 --> 00:17:20.220
He's a man, a real one!

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:22.630
Hurry up, Jim!
It's gonna get cold!

00:17:22.630 --> 00:17:23.370
I'm coming!

00:17:23.870 --> 00:17:27.190
What luck!
My stomach was growling!

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:43.710
I'm starving, Benbow.

00:17:47.350 --> 00:17:49.250
I'm going to eat some apples.

00:18:03.230 --> 00:18:04.640
Let's see...

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.600
That's all that's left?

00:18:07.600 --> 00:18:10.570
Oh well, this should be enough for me—

00:18:14.640 --> 00:18:16.190
Man, that hurt.

00:18:31.290 --> 00:18:33.810
Billy Bones was the first mate...

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:35.710
...and Flint was the captain.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:41.350
Additionally, our leader today is
none other than their helmsman.

00:18:42.800 --> 00:18:46.790
There were also men like
Blind Pew and Black Dog—

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.770
a real bunch of daredevils.

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:51.610
Right, boss?
Weren't there?

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.730
Yeah, you're absolutely right, Hands.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:11.280
Anyway, having one more man can't hurt.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:12.500
Carry on, Hands.

00:19:12.940 --> 00:19:15.460
S-Sure.
You listening, Puppy?

00:19:15.910 --> 00:19:20.470
As you already know, we were well
underway of cooking up a dirty trick.

00:19:20.470 --> 00:19:23.470
You know, it was to prevent
the rumor from spreading...

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:26.210
...that we organized that little race last night.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:30.850
And all that was done under the instruction of our boss, Silver.

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:33.630
What a surprise, a big surprise.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:36.820
I would've never thought that Mr. Silver was your boss.

00:19:36.820 --> 00:19:39.830
Our plan has been ready since the departure.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:42.660
Whether it's me, the boatswain Anderson...

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:44.320
...or old Morgan.

00:19:44.320 --> 00:19:48.880
We are all here thanks to good old Captain Silver.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:52.000
As for our plan...

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:56.390
It consists of letting this idiot Trelawney
lead us right to the treasure.

00:19:56.390 --> 00:20:00.110
Then, we'll get rid of them and split up the loot.

00:20:00.110 --> 00:20:06.050
After all, it's only natural that Captain Flint's treasure should be passed down to his "descendants".

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:06.560
Right?

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:09.620
Yes, of course.
It's all natural!

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:15.260
Consequently, Puppy the seagull.

00:20:15.260 --> 00:20:18.590
Now that you know our secret,
you have to join us.

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:22.630
Understood. I'm yours.
Whatever you wish.

00:20:23.280 --> 00:20:26.190
Good, you're quick to understand.
That's perfect.

00:20:26.190 --> 00:20:30.500
There you go, boss.
With him, that makes twenty!

00:20:32.870 --> 00:20:37.230
Put some heart into your work, Puppy, and you'll get a good share.

00:20:37.230 --> 00:20:39.210
Yes, gladly.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.790
Puppy, for your information,

00:20:41.790 --> 00:20:45.760
know that the great Flint himself was our high-esteemed leader.

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:48.010
So you must obey him.

00:20:48.010 --> 00:20:50.140
Y-Yes, I understand.

00:20:50.710 --> 00:20:53.750
<i>I-It's not possible!
It can't be Silver...</i>

00:20:53.750 --> 00:20:55.790
<i>My friend, John Silver...</i>

00:20:55.790 --> 00:20:59.770
<i>He was the cursed one-legged man that Billy Bones feared!</i>

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:03.670
By the way, Captain Silver?

00:21:03.670 --> 00:21:07.910
It would help if little Jim joined us, too, right?

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:11.150
Good idea! That kid is very close to Trelawney.

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:14.870
He would be very useful.
And our leader is close to him.

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:15.620
Shut up!

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:16.850
'K-Kay...

00:21:18.430 --> 00:21:21.310
Stop saying such nonsense about Jim.

00:21:21.310 --> 00:21:22.840
You'll follow my orders!

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.010
Y-Yes.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:25.340
Sorry, boss.

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:30.890
I'm starting to get hungry.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:32.030
Yeah.

00:21:32.030 --> 00:21:35.730
"Seagull" Puppy, hand me some apples, will you?

00:21:35.730 --> 00:21:37.790
Sure, right away.

00:21:43.950 --> 00:21:45.530
Land!

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:48.990
Land ho!
It's Treasure Island!

00:21:57.110 --> 00:21:59.670
What?!
Did you say Treasure Island?

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:27.360
Treasure Island! Treasure Island!

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:28.520
It's Treasure Island!

00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:31.620
To      be        continued

00:22:28.520 --> 00:22:30.110
Treasure Island! Treasure Island!

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:37.570
shiokaze yo omae mo

00:22:32.530 --> 00:22:37.570
Hey sea breeze

00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:43.380
tomodachi naraba tsutaete

00:22:37.570 --> 00:22:43.380
If you're my friend then carry

00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:49.590
furusato ni nokoshite kita

00:22:44.600 --> 00:22:49.590
To my home that I've left behind

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:55.030
natsukashii haha ni hitokoto

00:22:49.590 --> 00:22:55.030
A word to my dear mother

00:22:55.030 --> 00:23:00.440
boku wa genki de yattemasu

00:22:55.030 --> 00:23:00.440
Tell her that I'm doing fine

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:05.900
kaban ippai no

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:05.900
And that my bag filled

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:11.530
nozomi to yume to takaramono

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:11.530
With hopes, dreams and treasures

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:17.390
kakaete kaeritai

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:17.390
Will be brought back

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:23.980
yuuyake wo senaka ni

00:23:18.480 --> 00:23:23.980
The sunset on my back

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:29.870
kamome wo kata ni tomarasete

00:23:23.980 --> 00:23:29.870
And a seagull perched on my shoulder

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:39.590
boku wa fukimasu kuchibue wo

00:23:29.870 --> 00:23:39.590
I blow out a whistle

00:23:44.230 --> 00:23:46.970
It's impossible!
Silver's a pirate!

00:23:46.970 --> 00:23:48.410
I still can't believe it!

00:23:49.080 --> 00:23:50.820
Once we land,

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:54.530
I break away from the pirates
to scout ahead!

00:23:55.100 --> 00:23:57.740
What a responsibility.
My heart is pounding.

00:23:58.290 --> 00:24:00.070
That's when I bear witness.

00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:03.070
In the middle of the jungle,
Silver and his friends bear their fangs.

00:24:03.570 --> 00:24:04.920
Next time on Treasure Island:

00:24:04.920 --> 00:24:07.250
"Is Something Going Down on Treasure Island!?"

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:08.910
You're gonna be surprised!

